*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Target: Editor/Assembler
*
* Builds     dist/ea/{{TINAME}}O   tagged object, for option 3
*            dist/ea/{{TINAME}}    memory image, for option 5
* Requires   Editor/Assembler cartridge + 32K expansion + disk
*
* Relocatable, so the loader places it wherever there is room.
*
* Option 3 asks for a program name and finds it through DEF, so it needs
* no help. Option 5 has no entry field in its header at all - it simply
* begins executing at the address it loaded to. MAIN is not the first
* thing emitted, because the body starts with equates and the utility
* routines, so BOOT sits at offset 0 and jumps to it.
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
       DEF  MAIN

BOOT   B    @MAIN            * Entry for loaders that jump to offset 0

       COPY "../main.a99"
